Built and deployed 2026-09-21 (branch `worktree-admin-plan-elevation`, fast-
forwarded into main as cdce3a4fa; worker `2026-09-21T07-31-40-739Z`, web
`muaxfruf`, stripe-webhook redeployed; iPhone OTA build **202609210829**
published, Alice **202609210847**; install from Settings > Advanced > Builds
— the phone was unreachable for a direct install).

**The hole that prompted it:** the Stripe webhook worker served `POST /test`
with NO authentication — any `{userId, tier}` body set that Clerk user's
`subscriptionTier`. Anyone with a user id could make any account Enterprise
(which carries `account:team_management`). The web Admin tab's "simulate tier
change" buttons were its only legitimate caller. Route + handler deleted;
`POST /test` now falls through to the signed-webhook path and returns 400
"Missing signature".

**Replacement:** `PATCH /admin/users/:userId/plan` in the API worker, router-
gated on `admin:manage_users`. Body `{ tier?: free|pro|enterprise, role?:
admin|user }`. Merges Clerk `public_metadata` via
`updateClerkUserPublicMetadata` (auth/clerk.ts; Clerk deep-merges, `null`
deletes a key — that is how `role: 'user'` removes admin). Writes
`planSource: 'manual'`, `planSetBy`, `planSetAt`. Refuses an admin removing
their own role (400). Tests: `packages/api/src/admin/plan.test.ts`.

**Manual plan = floor.** stripe-webhook `updateClerkUserMetadata` now reads
current metadata first; if `planSource === 'manual'` and the incoming billing
tier is <= the manual tier, it skips the write (logs "Keeping manual … plan").
A billing event that RAISES the tier writes it with `planSource: 'billing'`
and owns it from then on. Setting tier to `free` manually ends a comp. A Clerk
read failure never blocks a billing write. `GET /admin/users` projects
`planSource`.

  }
  if (tier !== undefined && !PLAN_TIERS.includes(tier)) {
    return errorResponse(400, 'Invalid tier. Must be free, pro, or enterprise');
  }
  if (role !== undefined && role !== 'admin' && role !== 'user') {
    return errorResponse(400, "Invalid role. Must be 'admin' or 'user'");
  }

  // The last admin removing their own role has no way back in except the
  // Clerk dashboard. Refuse it here rather than discover it at sign-in.
  if (role === 'user' && userId === ctx.userId) {
    return errorResponse(400, 'You cannot remove your own admin role');
  }

  const existing = await fetchClerkUser(userId, env);
  if (!existing) {
    return errorResponse(404, 'User not found');
  }

  const now = new Date().toISOString();
  const patch: Record<string, unknown> = { updatedAt: now };
  if (tier !== undefined) {
    patch.subscriptionTier = tier;
    patch.planSource = 'manual';
    patch.planSetBy = ctx.userId;
    patch.planSetAt = now;
  }
  if (role !== undefined) {
    // null deletes the key in Clerk's merge, which is exactly "not an admin".
    patch.role = role === 'admin' ? 'admin' : null;
  }

  const updated = await updateClerkUserPublicMetadata(userId, patch, env);
  if (!updated) {
    return errorResponse(502, 'Clerk rejected the update');
  }

  console.log(
    `[Admin] ${ctx.userId} set plan for ${userId}:`,
    JSON.stringify({ tier, role })
  );

  const response: UpdateUserPlanResponse = {
    userId,
    tier: updated.public_metadata?.subscriptionTier ?? tier ?? 'free',
    role: updated.public_metadata?.role ?? null,
    planSource: updated.public_metadata?.planSource ?? null,
    updatedAt: now,
  };
  return new Response(JSON.stringify(response), {
    status: 200,
    headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json', 'Cache-Control': 'no-store' },
  });
}

