---
name: project_cms_delegated_design
description: "CMS delegated per-site design mode — a site-key member (not a global admin) can design one portal, layout-only"
metadata: 
  node_type: memory
  type: project
  originSessionId: 77554904-05d2-4a39-b1e6-b31ab3437230
---

Delegated CMS design: a site-key **member** (not a global Ripul/Clerk admin) can enter CMS design mode for ONE portal, scoped to the site they entered through the CMS domain. Shipped 2026-07-01 (commits a13069b2d server, 285a3ca1c client, a5a0e6c6b config UI).

**Mechanism** (mirrors the per-site data-plane gates [[project_role_page_visibility]] / canEditTable):
- `CmsDefinition.designRoles: string[]` — site-key roles allowed to design. Set in the definition settings panel (CmsDefinitionEditContent designRoles multiselect). Empty ⇒ admin-only (every existing site unchanged).
- `GET /v1/site-key/me` returns server-computed `canDesign` (owner.role ∈ designRoles). Client gate = `isAdmin || membership.canDesign` in PortalPage; feeds EditablePortalBlocks via both DirectPageRender and the shell `pageOutlet` path.
- Write: **new** `PATCH /v1/cms-definitions/:cmsId/design` (runtime, site-key-scoped, mirrors `/v1/.../posts`). Requires clerk_jwt; re-authorizes fails-closed: acting `body.siteKeyId` must resolve to :cmsId (direct or delegateCmsDefinitionTo), caller must be a site_key_owner of it with role ∈ designRoles. Applies LAYOUT ONLY (pages/components/theme/portalConfig/scripts/columnViews/page pointers) — never queries/mutations/tables/relationships/connections/authProviders/designRoles. Returns minimal ack (no config disclosure).
- Delegated designer's EditablePortalBlocks seeds from the portal payload (DelegatedDesignInfo.seed), NOT the admin GET (403 for non-admins); saves via `updatePortalDesign()`; skips the admin site-key picker.

**Key decisions**: layout-only carve-out is the RLS/credential/escalation guard the user flagged (a designer must NOT be able to rewrite RLS or widen their own grant). NO implicit bypass for site-key owner/admin roles — design is opt-in per role (only the GLOBAL Clerk admin auto-designs). Identity decoupled from authz.

**BYOA designers work too** (commit 85e5a279e, deployed 2026-07-01). On a true BYOA portal (e.g. business.wac.rocks) there is NO Ripul login — users auth via the customer IdP (portalAuth.jwksUrl). BYOA token verification is wired PER-ROUTE in index.ts (query/mutation-run branch ~1382, /me branch ~1397); added a matching PATCH /design branch (derive site key from cmsId, retry verifyClerkJwt with portalAuth.jwksUrl). Key: resolveForUser stamps authSource:'clerk_jwt' for ANY verified user, so once the BYOA token verifies, the /design route gate passes and the handler authorizes by verified email → design role. Client needs nothing — useCmsDefinitionsService already forces allowSiteKeyToken:false, so it sends the customer token (not the site-key token). So a WAC user with a design role designs business.wac.rocks logged in AS THEMSELVES. Grant = designRoles + their email is a site_key_owner/directory member with that role.

Two hosting models: Ripul-hosted portal (acme.ripul.io) → designer signs in with Ripul Clerk. BYOA portal (business.wac.rocks) → designer signs in with customer IdP, matched by email. Both work.

DEPLOYED (demo.ripul.io). Worker package tsgo is pre-existing RED on main (customDomains/buildStoredConnection/etc.) — unrelated; my code compiled clean.
    // Site Key Owner Management Routes (requires admin:manage_site_keys permission)
    // ========================================================================

    // Route: GET/POST /admin/site-keys/:id/owners
    const siteKeyOwnersMatch = path.match(/^\/admin\/site-keys\/([^/]+)\/owners$/);
    if (siteKeyOwnersMatch) {
      if (!PermissionResolver.hasPermission(authContext, 'admin:manage_site_keys')) {
        const response = errorResponse(403, 'Permission denied: admin:manage_site_keys required');
        return addCorsHeaders(response, origin, env);
      }
      if (request.method === 'GET') {
        const response = await handleListSiteKeyOwners(siteKeyOwnersMatch[1], authContext, env);
        return addCorsHeaders(response, origin, env);
      }
      if (request.method === 'POST') {
        const response = await handleAddSiteKeyOwner(siteKeyOwnersMatch[1], request, authContext, env);
        return addCorsHeaders(response, origin, env);
      }
    }

    // Route: PATCH/DELETE /admin/site-keys/:id/owners/:userId
    const siteKeyOwnerMatch = path.match(/^\/admin\/site-keys\/([^/]+)\/owners\/([^/]+)$/);
    if (siteKeyOwnerMatch) {
      if (!PermissionResolver.hasPermission(authContext, 'admin:manage_site_keys')) {
        const response = errorResponse(403, 'Permission denied: admin:manage_site_keys required');
        return addCorsHeaders(response, origin, env);
      }
      // The userId segment is URL-encoded by the client. BYOA-by-email rows
      // have ids like `byoa:user@host.com` (→ `byoa%3Auser%40host.com`), so
      // without decoding the WHERE user_id = ? lookup matches 0 rows and the
      // update silently no-ops. The site-key id segment is alphanumeric.
      const ownerSiteKeyId = siteKeyOwnerMatch[1];
      const ownerUserId = decodeURIComponent(siteKeyOwnerMatch[2]);
      if (request.method === 'PATCH') {
        const response = await handleUpdateSiteKeyOwner(ownerSiteKeyId, ownerUserId, request, authContext, env);
        return addCorsHeaders(response, origin, env);
      }
      if (request.method === 'DELETE') {
        const response = await handleRemoveSiteKeyOwner(ownerSiteKeyId, ownerUserId, authContext, env);
        return addCorsHeaders(response, origin, env);
      }
    }

